  "prefLabel": "He-M 306.04 Criteria for Emergency Treatment",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "He-M 306.04 Criteria for Emergency Treatment. A licensed practitioner requesting authorization to administer emergency treatment shall demonstrate, by clear and convincing evidence, that:\n\n(a) A medical or psychiatric emergency exists;\n\n(b) The patient’s admission status is one of the following:\n\n(1) A district court found probable cause for involuntary emergency admission pursuant to RSA 135-C:27-33;\n\n(2) A probate court ordered involuntary admission pursuant to RSA 135-C:34-45; or\n\n(3) New Hampshire hospital has absolutely revoked the patient’s conditional discharge in accordance with RSA 135-C:51 and He-M 609.06 due, at least in part, to the patient’s dangerousness;\n\n(c) The patient does not have a guardian authorized to make medical decisions;\n\n(d) The involuntarily admitted patient cannot make a decision regarding their treatment due to lack of capacity; and\n\n(e) A reasonable person would consent to the administration of emergency treatment.\n\nSource. #3096, eff 8-19-85; EXPIRED: 8-19-91\n\nNew. #4708, eff 12-1-89, EXPIRED: 12-1-95\n\nNew. #7133, eff 11-23-99; ss by #7559, eff 9-25-01; ss by #9520, eff 8-4-09; ss by #10641, eff 7-18-14, EXPIRED: 7-18-24\n\nNew. #14637, eff 6-26-26, EXPIRES: 6-26-36",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/he-m300.html"
